B.ayW=new A.ia("Chip-8","A virtual machine that implements the Chip-8 instruction set. It handles a memory map of 4KB, 16 general-purpose registers, a dedicated program counter, and a stack for subroutine calls. The emulator manages the 60Hz delay and sound timers while rendering the monochrome display buffer using SDL2.\n\n\nC \u2022 CHIP8 \u2022 emulation \u2022 SDL2","https://github.com/carlosvts/chip8",null)
B.az1=new A.ia("Bitmap parser","A zero-dependency parser designed to read and manipulate BMP files at the byte level. It extracts file headers and pixel arrays into raw buffers, allowing for the application of manual convolution kernels to perform image filtering operations like gausian blur and Sobel's edge detection without external libraries.\n\n\nC++ \u2022 parsing \u2022 image processing \u2022 image filtering","https://github.com/carlosvts/raw-image-processor",null)
B.ayU=new A.ia("Malloc implementation","A custom dynamic memory allocator that provides implementations for malloc, calloc, realloc, and free. It interacts with the Linux kernel via the sbrk syscall and manages the heap segment using a doubly linked list structure to track allocated and free memory blocks, handling block splitting and merging.\n\n\nC \u2022 memory \u2022 syscalls \u2022 low-level","https://github.com/carlosvts/malloc-implementation",null)
B.az0=new A.ia("Input multiplexer","A Linux utility that monitors multiple input event devices simultaneously (Mouse and Keyboard). It uses the epoll system call to implement an asynchronous I/O multiplexing loop, reading raw event structures from /dev/input/ and parsing hexadecimal data from keyboard and mouse devices in a single-threaded execution flow. Can be expanded into almost any device at /dev/input \n\n\nC++ \u2022 Linux \u2022 epoll \u2022 concurrency \u2022 evdev","https://github.com/carlosvts/input-multiplexer",null)
B.ayZ=new A.ia("HTTP Server","A multi-threaded HTTP/1.1 server built using the Linux socket API. It manually handles the TCP handshake, parses raw string requests into method/path components, and constructs valid HTTP response headers and body payloads. Concurrency is managed through a thread-per-connection model using POSIX threads.\n\nC++ \u2022 Sockets \u2022 HTTP/1.1 \u2022 Linux \u2022 Network","https://github.com/carlosvts/http-server-cpp",null)
B.ayV=new A.ia("Raytracer","A 2D raycasting engine that calculates light and shadow visibility through geometric intersections. It casts rays from a central source and computes the nearest collision point with environment segments using linear algebra, rendering the resulting visibility polygon into an SFML window buffer.\n\n\nC++ \u2022 graphics \u2022 math \u2022 SFML \u2022 geometry","https://github.com/carlosvts/raytracing",null)
B.ayY=new A.ia("Sandbox Game","A real-time physics simulation based on cellular automata rules. Each pixel in the grid acts as an individual element with specific density and state properties. The engine updates the grid every frame, calculating interactions between falling solids, flowing liquids, and expanding gases based on neighbor-state logic.\n\n\nC++ \u2022 engine \u2022 physics \u2022 simulation \u2022 Raylib","https://github.com/carlosvts/sandbox-game",null)
B.ayX=new A.ia("Game of Life","An implementation of Conway's Game of Life that simulates cellular evolution on a discrete 2D grid. The program applies the four standard transition rules to each cell state simultaneously and uses SFML to render the grid, allowing for real-time interaction with the initial seed. \n\n\nC++ \u2022 SFML \u2022 simulation \u2022 cellular automata","https://github.com/carlosvts/GameOfLife",null)
B.az_=new A.ia("Portfolio","The source code for this web-based portfolio. It is built using the Flutter framework and Dart, focusing on a custom layout architecture to showcase low-level C++ projects. The deployment is automated via GitHub Actions, serving the compiled JavaScript and CanvasKit assets through GitHub Pages.\n\nFlutter \u2022 Dart \u2022 Portfolio \u2022 Web development","https://github.com/carlosvts/portfolio",null)
